From 87f209cdcfd30b993613d31be0dab06bc5811e34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:30:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09462/11362] [outer-loop] Truthful archival: derive task
 results from evidence, refuse duplicate milestone appends
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REQ-CONDUCTOR-ARCHIVE-1 (renamed from the spec commit's REQ-INFRA-6500:
the live milestone already uses experiment ids 6500/6501, so REQ ids in
that numeric range would collide with the experiment-numbered
convention; the spec-coverage regex also requires a numeric tail).

_archive_current_milestone (both definitions — the first is shadowed
dead code, updated anyway so no phantom literal survives a reorder) now
derives each task result from the conductor log's own rows plus
deliverable existence, and refuses to append a milestone id
research-complete.yaml already holds. The hardcoded 'OK (conductor)'
literal is gone: it had certified 57 tasks whose deliverables were never
created, and the unconditional append produced 684 copies of milestone
.510.

Takes effect on the conductor's next natural restart.

